    "reviewed_findings": [
      "The final main page and eight trait variant pages match the actual eight variants and eighteen inventory/UI bindings. All eight trait IDs appear on their matching variant page; every bound mark name appears in WEAPON_COMPATIBILITY; each matching weapon reverse index contains its trait ID.",
      "The own-tier receipt supports seven families at 0.24/0.28/0.32/0.36 and the Transonic Sword at 0.09/0.12/0.15/0.18, all with 3.5-second duration. Each actual wrapper has one direct clone of the common base; same-key own tiers replace the fallback. The formatter adds a plus prefix for seven families and not for the Transonic Sword, matching the tier table and reconstruction.",
      "Trigger and timing text accurately distinguishes a same-item melee hit ordinal of at least three from arbitrary contacts, excludes pure push and sticky secondary profiles, and states that the third hit resolves before queued processing. The 3.5-second window refreshes without stacking or cooldown; the held gate disables the bonus while switched away, and removal on unequip is described.",
      "The damage and math pages treat the modifier as post-Power-Type-curve melee power input affecting attack, impact, and cleave calculations rather than a fixed final-damage percentage. The controlled 100→136 and 100→118 examples identify the selected tier and preserve profile/downstream caveats.",
      "The EN/ZH RAW keys and SHA match the verification receipt. The static reconstruction lists all four tiers for both formatter families; rule comparison distinguishes actual runtime conditions from details the RAW does not cover. The fixed image attachment, shared map entry, and reverse indexes agree with the canonical config."
    ],
